<task id="130" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>H3: Graph app-reg port (Applications/ServicePrincipals/AppRoleAssignedTo/Oauth2PermissionGrants) + real consent verifier + KV writes + H10-idiom app-user assign</title>
    <phase>C'' Wave G-3 -- Identity + deploy</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Heaviest single port in the whole Phase G'' backlog per DS-1b (982-line script, 14 grants, consent flow) -- security-sensitive (Entra app registration, consent gate). FULL rigor.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Named explicitly in the parent task instructions' xhigh-effort exception list: 'complex-but-fully-specified... H3 heavy port' -- Sonnet @ xhigh.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>102, 103, 125, 126</deps>
    <tags>l2-controlplane, job-handler, option-d, sdk-port, auth</tags>
    <estimated-effort>14-20 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Port H3EntraAppRegHandler.cs's collaborator RegisterEntraAppRegScriptProvisioner (Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1, 982 lines: az ad app x19, az ad sp x2, az rest [Graph] x3, az keyvault secret x3, pac admin assign-app-to-environment x1) to Microsoft.Graph 6.x (already a BFF dependency at 6.5.0): Applications.PostAsync for app registration, ServicePrincipals for SP creation, AppRoleAssignedTo for the 14 grants, Oauth2PermissionGrants for delegated-permission wiring; KV writes via SecretClient (task 125's collaborator); the lone `pac admin assign-app-to-environment` call maps to the EXACT SAME Dataverse Web API app-user creation H10's collaborators already perform in-process (DataverseWebApiAppUserCreator.cs idiom -- REUSE it, do not reimplement). ALSO replace NullAdminConsentVerifier (which always returns Verified -- the consent gate can currently advance on fiction) with a real implementation: ONE Graph oauth2PermissionGrants query (~80 LOC per DS-1b) that actually checks whether admin consent was granted.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Microsoft.Graph 6.x Applications/ServicePrincipals/AppRoleAssignments/Oauth2PermissionGrants SDK surface, Entra app-registration idempotency, and admin-consent verification via oauth2PermissionGrants queries.</role>

  <goal>H3EntraAppRegHandler.cs's provisioner is a pure Microsoft.Graph SDK implementation performing: app-reg ensure (idempotent create-if-absent), SP ensure, the 14 AppRoleAssignedTo grants (per GraphAppRoles.cs's completed 11-of-14 catalog, task 005), Oauth2PermissionGrants wiring, KV writes, and Dataverse app-user assignment via the REUSED H10 idiom. A real AdminConsentVerifier replaces NullAdminConsentVerifier, performing a genuine Graph query proving consent was granted (not assumed). Recipe order per DS-4 §3: Graph app ensure -&gt; 14 AppRoleAssignedTo grants -&gt; consent gate -&gt; real Oauth2PermissionGrants verify -&gt; KV writes -&gt; Dataverse app-user assign.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-1b classifies H3's collaborator as 'the single heaviest port' (8-10 person-days per DS-1b §5) among all Class-A handlers. DS-4 §3 (H3 deep-dive) is explicit about the current defect's severity: 'POML 046 disclosed the Null consent verifier in scaffold headers, but the handler BEHAVES AS IF consent is verified (gate can advance on fiction).' This is distinct from an honestly-disclosed interim state -- it is a gate that silently passes. DS-4's recipe order (app ensure -&gt; 14 grants -&gt; consent gate -&gt; real verify -&gt; KV -&gt; Dataverse assign) is the authoritative sequencing this task follows. The 11-of-14 GraphAppRoles.cs GUIDs are already complete (task 005); the remaining 3 are a pre-existing, separately-tracked project risk item, not this task's scope to complete.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/EntraAppReg/H3EntraAppRegHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/EntraAppReg/GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/EntraAppReg/GraphAdminConsentVerifier.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/EntraAppReg/NullAdminConsentVerifier.cs (retire)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">scripts/Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/DataverseAppUserGraphParity/DataverseWebApiAppUserCreator.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Auth/GraphAppRoles.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="102" status="pending">wave-sequencing</dependency>
      <dependency task="103" status="pending">H3 keyed registration</dependency>
      <dependency task="125" status="pending">H4's SecretClient collaborator this task reuses for KV writes must exist</dependency>
      <dependency task="126" status="pending">H4's real-value-sourcing fix must have landed so the KV values H3 reads/writes are functional, not placeholder</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="design.md §4.1b">Handler runtime classification (Option D hybrid, DS-1b Sec.2): 12 handlers are pure .NET SDK/REST under DefaultAzureCredential pinned to the L2 UAMI (Class A); H14a is the sole Class-C residual (Exchange sidecar); H7/H10/H11/H12c are already native. No ProcessStartInfo/shell-out collaborator may remain in this handler's target state.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md MUST rules (post-line-254 block)">No new ProcessStartInfo/shell-out collaborator may be introduced by this task. Option D's entire point is deleting the pwsh/az/pac dependency from the L2 runtime, not adding to it (the sole designed exception is the H14a Exchange sidecar).</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-4 §3 H3 deep-dive">Recipe order is binding, not incidental: Graph app ensure -&gt; 14 AppRoleAssignedTo grants -&gt; consent gate -&gt; real Oauth2PermissionGrants verify -&gt; KV writes -&gt; Dataverse app-user assign via the H10 idiom. Do not reorder (e.g., writing KV secrets before consent verification would leak a functional secret before the consent gate has genuinely passed).</constraint>
    <constraint source="this project's CLAUDE.md MUST rules">MUST complete 11 of 14 null AppRoleId GUIDs in GraphAppRoles.cs BEFORE first production customer -- already done (task 005). This task consumes the completed catalog; it does NOT re-verify or re-complete the GUIDs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-4 §3">REUSE the H10 Dataverse app-user creation idiom verbatim for the pac admin assign-app-to-environment replacement -- do not write a second, parallel implementation of the same find-by-applicationid/create/role-associate sequence.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>H3 Graph app-reg port + real consent verifier</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds1b-option-d-hybrid-deep-dive.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Idempotent App User registration (reuse, not reimplement)" location="src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/DataverseAppUserGraphParity/DataverseWebApiAppUserCreator.cs">The exact find-by-applicationid/create-if-absent/role-associate sequence H3's Dataverse-assign step reuses verbatim per DS-4's explicit instruction.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL, xhigh effort). Read Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 in FULL (982 lines) plus GraphAppRoles.cs's completed catalog and DataverseWebApiAppUserCreator.cs in full.</step>
    <step order="1" name="App-reg + SP ensure">Author GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner: idempotent Applications.PostAsync (find-by-displayName or a tracked appId first) + ServicePrincipals ensure.</step>
    <step order="2" name="14 grants">Wire the 14 AppRoleAssignedTo grants per GraphAppRoles.cs's completed catalog.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Real consent verifier">Author GraphAdminConsentVerifier: query Oauth2PermissionGrants, assert the expected scope set is present -- replace NullAdminConsentVerifier's unconditional Verified with this real check. WaitingOnGate is the correct outcome when consent is genuinely not yet granted (external human latency, per DS-4b's wall-clock analysis -- this is a session-free wait, not a bug).</step>
    <step order="4" name="KV writes">Wire H4's SecretClient collaborator (task 125) for H3's own KV writes (the app-reg client secret, etc.).</step>
    <step order="5" name="Dataverse app-user assign">Reuse DataverseWebApiAppUserCreator's exact idiom (either by direct reuse of the class, or a thin H3-scoped wrapper calling into the same underlying sequence) for the pac admin assign-app-to-environment replacement.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Wire up">Replace RegisterEntraAppRegScriptProvisioner and NullAdminConsentVerifier in H3's owning module with the new real implementations.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Parity tests">Author acceptance tests asserting parity against recorded script outputs (DS-1b §6's mitigation for the heavy-port risk class) -- at minimum, the 14-grant set + the app-reg idempotency (re-run = no-op) + the real-vs-fake consent-gate branching.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Build + verify">dotnet build 0 errors; dotnet test green.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any of the 14 AppRoleAssignedTo grants targets a GraphAppRoles.cs entry that is STILL a null GUID (one of the 3 not-yet-completed per task 005's 11-of-14 status), STOP and escalate per this project's existing risk-register entry rather than skipping that grant silently — a skipped grant is a silent T3-class failure exactly like the risk register warns.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the real GraphAdminConsentVerifier's query shape does not match what NullAdminConsentVerifier's callers expect (e.g., a WaitingOnGate outcome the handler's state machine doesn't have a transition for), STOP and escalate to confirm the gate-state contract with the dispatcher/reconciler design (tasks 102/104) before shipping a verifier whose real outcomes the handler can't correctly route.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build/test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/EntraAppReg/GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/EntraAppReg/GraphAdminConsentVerifier.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">grep 'ProcessStartInfo\|Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1' in the new H3 collaborator files returns 0 matches.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test confirms all 14 AppRoleAssignedTo grants are attempted against GraphAppRoles.cs's completed catalog entries (11 real GUIDs; the 3 still-null entries are explicitly skipped WITH a loud warning, not silently dropped).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GraphAdminConsentVerifier test: given a fake Oauth2PermissionGrants response WITHOUT the expected scope set, the verifier returns NOT-Verified (WaitingOnGate), not Verified -- proving the gate can no longer advance on fiction.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GraphAdminConsentVerifier test: given a fake Oauth2PermissionGrants response WITH the expected scope set, the verifier returns Verified.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Dataverse app-user assignment step reuses (via direct call or thin wrapper) DataverseWebApiAppUserCreator's exact idiom -- grep confirms no duplicate find-by-applicationid/create/associate implementation exists in H3's new files.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- Microsoft.Graph 6.5.0 is already a BFF dependency and DataverseWebApiAppUserCreator already implements the exact app-user idiom H3's last step needs; nothing new to invent for those two pieces. Extension -- porting the remaining 982-line script's app-reg/grant/consent logic to Graph SDK calls, while REUSING (not reimplementing) the app-user step, is the correct minimal-duplication extension. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- H3 cannot execute under Option D's zero-shell main site; separately, and more dangerously, the consent gate currently 'behaves as if consent is verified' when it is not -- a customer's admin consent could be silently assumed-granted, an auth-integrity defect DS-4 calls out as worse than a mere missing feature.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
